299 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In the late stages of training, around 80 to 100 epochs, the generator becomes highly skilled at producing near-photorealistic outputs. By this time, it has successfully learned two important things: first, to match the overall structure of the target image using the L1 loss; second, to create realistic small textures like trees, windows, and roads using the adversarial GAN loss. As a result, the images generated are almost indistinguishable from real photos, showing sharp edges, correct shapes, and natural colors. The training stabilizes at this point because both the generator and discriminator have become strong opponents, constantly improving against each other. This leads to high-quality, realistic images that maintain both global consistency and fine local details.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
